+## Latest native panel, route-placement and selection corrections
+
+The latest draft builds the 1-Up match view from private instances of the game's `Throwdowns_Details_Page`, Throwdown details stack panel, native Quit button and native scoreboard. Its HUD prompt uses the game's Throwdown Panel action and controller glyph; the game's pause state retains phone pose, input ownership and Back behavior. Players and Turn Timer appear in the information panel with the 1-Up title and private blue badge. Quit is tied to the current match. The page mount retains its prior presenter and restores it only while that slot still belongs to the private panel, so tab changes or newer native content are not overwritten. Partial construction rolls back owned models, and an unavailable panel retains the working native quit path for recovery. This is an implementation change awaiting live confirmation, not a claim that the requested panel has been visually tested.
+
+Deathrace placement instructions now use separate native LabelButton prompts with native input-action references, controller glyphs and the game's font in a bounded screen-margin layout. The long overflowing text line is removed. The controls retain LT/RT object switching, primary-action placement, D-pad rotation/save/undo and native Back. Placement ground rays run on the client update before the park-editor store-ready guard; a missing park-editor store no longer prevents route cursor ground hits. Native gate validation no longer rejects the destroy entry point merely because ReSkate already installed its verified shared entity-lifetime detour. Other native ABI checks remain in place.
+
+Reopening setup compares the game's active body with the retained private body and remounts the latter when native construction restores stock contents. This preserves Deathrace's Players and Timer rows, its 60-second initial timer and the existing private selections instead of reintroducing Join, Invite and Rounds. A verified new picker action also retires an abandoned unconfirmed cleanup state when there is no actual flag/MMID. Active flag placement and registered matches retain their ownership protections. These changes address the reported once-only setup and changed-layout failures without mutating shared stock challenge models.
+
+The pulse authoring investigation found two concrete defects: the conditional gate used the interpolator's `Out` hash rather than the conditional entity's native `Output` hash, and the draft cleared compiled-cache fields on RimeWidgetEntityData instead of their owning RimeWidgetBlueprint. The corrected private gate routes `Output` (`-1399230854`) to the prefab's public `Out` field, and the private Blueprint clears ClientSchematics/ServerSchematics with bus offset 65535, matching authored native graph widgets. The native real-time sine interpolation uses 0.9-second legs, scale 1.0–1.06 and idle identity. Re-read serialized checks verify the output gate, hover/focus activation, both selected visual transforms, startup polarity, lifetime events, feedback and cache removal. Native typed ContentPresenterTileViewModel binding and all stock cached paths remain unchanged.
+
+Fresh asset artifacts are in `../../outputs/Throwdown-artwork/pulse-fix-20261010/` and `../../outputs/Throwdown-artwork/compiled-pulse-fix-20261010/Patch`. The CLI Release build, native asset authoring and mod compilation succeeded with 104 resources, 12 bundles and 10 TOCs. The eight-material checkpoint shader subset remains isolated; no shared world shader depot or new artwork iteration was added. Evidence uses `../pulse-fix-` logs and `../pulse-fix-20261010.md`.
