+## Empty setup body and placement controls regression repair
+
+The user confirmed that the selection pulse now works and looks good. That approved native asset archive is unchanged in this repair: SHA-256 `a0df97490c35bdefb9842b986be9a177e333ba0f83fc76db4cfb1ea61b97f86d`, 107,811,233 bytes. The rebuilt DLL's embedded resource was compared with the source archive without executing the DLL and matched exactly.
+
+The user then reported empty Throwdown setup bodies and an unusable Deathrace editor. The setup updater compared native array allocation addresses, but native array publication allocates separate storage. It therefore repeatedly republished the entire StackComponent and reset its native animation/focus state. It could also retain an empty body before the game's Players and Timer rows existed. Adaptation now waits for those rows, compares each Content presenter's blueprint/record/handle identity, and replaces only changed presenters while retaining the live StackItem visibility, transition and focus state. Restoration uses the same ownership checks. The native menu fixture covers separate allocations, 100 progressing animation frames, genuine reentry, each presenter identity field, changed item counts and malformed layouts.
